## 0. Overall verdict

**The fix is correct, does what it claims, and loosens nothing.** 222-directory batch, a 400-case
differential fuzz against an independent oracle, and 21 hand-built controls all agree. No case was
found where the new checker accepts something the old one rejected, and the claimed blind spot is
genuinely closed.

Findings are minor and none of them blocks the change: two inherited acceptance properties, one
anchoring observation, one **new cosmetic defect (spurious stderr)**, one wording overclaim in the
prior report, and one test-coverage gap.

